{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["The word הבה is like תנה; its root is יהב. Witness: \"Cast upon HaShem your burden\" (Psalm 55:23). Because it is spoken frequently, it is found in plural form: \"הבה נתחכמה\" (Exodus 1:10); also for the feminine: \"הבה נא אבוא אליך\" (Genesis 38:16)." "Do not wonder at the phrase \"its head in the heavens,\" for Moses spoke thus: \"cities great and fortified in the heavens\" (Deuteronomy 1:28). These builders saw in their counsel that they should not separate — and HaShem did not counsel so, and they did not know."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved ד' in the Psalm citation as HaShem per the standard abbreviation convention."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:08.598399077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}